bench_local30_gen.py is a benchmark script that generates answers for the       
Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B model using a local Ollama instance.                        

Key functionality:                                                              

 • Generates responses for the "hard-30" query set via Ollama's                 
   OpenAI-compatible endpoint                                                   
 • Uses 4-bit quantized model (runs on CPU/mac with ~18GB memory)               
 • Outputs results to eval_candidates_local30_hard.json                         
 • Implements resume capability (skips already-generated queries on             
   crash/restart)                                                               
 • Measures latency for each response                                           

Workflow:                                                                       

 1 Loads existing output file if present (for resume)                           
 2 Iterates through HARD_QUERY_SET prompts                                      
 3 Calls http_call() to Ollama endpoint with model, messages, timeout, and      
   max_tokens                                                                   
 4 Saves each answer incrementally to JSON                                      
 5 Reports success rate and output file path                                    

Purpose: To compare the local 30B model against the H200-served 80B model (from 
eval_candidates_specialist_hard.json) in a head-to-head grading scenario.       

